Register no Rust toolchains

The module registers a toolchain for every host and target triple its rust
extension provides, and each build configuration analyses all of them during
toolchain resolution. It is reached only through protobuf, and this build
compiles Rust with the toolchains rules_rs registers, whose toolchain type
belongs to rules_rs's own copy of rules_rust.

The patch removes four lines from the module's MODULE.bazel and carries the
six around them, too little of the file to attribute.

License: Apache-2.0 (rules_rust 0.69.0)

--- a/MODULE.bazel
+++ b/MODULE.bazel
@@ -47,10 +47,6 @@
 rust.toolchain(edition = "2021")
 use_repo(rust, "rust_toolchains")
 
-register_toolchains(
-    "@rust_toolchains//:all",
-)
-
 rust_host_tools = use_extension("//rust:extensions.bzl", "rust_host_tools")
 rust_host_tools.host_tools(
     name = "rust_host_tools",
